 "intro_html": "A whole strawberry is wrapped in a thin layer of <a href=\"anko.html\">anko</a>, then in a thin sheet of mochi. The mochi is shiratamako, sugar and water, cooked in the microwave in three short bursts and stirred in between. Cut one in half and you get the red ring of strawberry inside the dark anko and white mochi. Mochi goes hard in the fridge, so make them the day you eat them.",
